## Phase 3 — REPRODUCED both bugs (sandbox: real-DB copy, empty cwd, restored tabs)
Sandbox learnings (shape fidelity):
- Our roots are `opencode-rust`-suffixed (data AND state): tabs restore reads
  `$XDG_STATE_HOME/opencode-rust/stable/tui/tabs.json` (channel default "stable");
  v2 reads `.../opencode/latest|local/tui/tabs.json`. Both seeded per side.
- First our-binary boot in a v2-shaped home runs the one-way v2→rust DB migration
  (1.5G copy) — user's env has the marker; sandbox pre-seeded marker + DB.
- Ref must run WITHOUT bun defines (the TUI-spawned background server re-execs without
  them → channel skew local vs stable → discovery loop); ref DB = opencode-local.db.
- v2 tsconfig.json seeded in the empty cwd (the rig's jsxImportSource fix).

Evidence (80x24, cwd=/tmp/opencode/dogfood2/home/work, 2 restored tabs referencing
sessions whose directory is /opt/lobechat + /opt/new-api — none for the cwd):
- OURS boot: strip row0 painted (two tab titles + " + "). Composer input row = 14
  ("Ask anything…" row), hardware cursor = (6,13) → ONE ROW ABOVE the input row
  (= exactly the strip height; set_caret_cell ran before the strip shift).
- OURS click SGR col5 row1 (tab 1 body): NOTHING changes (same rows, same cursor).
- REF boot: strip row0 painted; input row = 13 (home lays out in height-1); cursor
  (6,13) ON the input row. REF same click: route switches to the session (renders
  its session card — "Session not found: …" for a cross-project session id, i.e.
  v2 routes even when the cwd's project scope can't see it).
- Extra divergence captured: ours lays home out at FULL height then truncates →
  bottom status row clipped (ours shows version row at 22; ref status bar at 23).

## Phase 4 — fix plan (1:1 v2 semantics)
- app.rs mouse_event: strip_live must include Route::Home (v2 app.tsx:576-579
  tabsAvailable gates on `route.data.type !== "plugin"` only + 1353-1355 app-wide mount).
- home.rs render_home: lay the home view out in height-1 when the strip shows (v2:
  strip is row 0 of the SAME column — app.tsx:1349-1361), prepend the strip row, and
  shift the caret cell +1 (caret inside the shifted subtree).

## Phase 5 — bug 3: boot model ignores config providers (Own/glm-5.3)
Real shape (sanitized probe of the live config): `providers.own` (camelCase keys,
package @opencode/ai/providers/anthropic, settings{apiKey,baseURL}, models with
cost as an ARRAY of {input,output}) + `model: "Own/glm-5.3"` + small_model.

ROOT CAUSE (ours only): the provider/model seeding read the global config from the
`opencode-rust`-suffixed dir — boot.rs:116 (engine seeding), boot.rs:297
(location_config), engine/mod.rs:534 (per-location assemble) — while every other
config consumer (handlers/config.rs:27, handlers/agent.rs:103, announce.rs:296) and
the REF read the SHARED v2 dir `~/.config/opencode`. Result: zero config providers
bound → `own` missing from /api/model (10 models vs ref's 38) → default fell to the
catalog fallback ("opencode zen fledge alpha free").
- normalize + provider decode are FINE (probe: providers.own + cost array + agents
  .title.model small_model migration all survive; matches ref /api/config exactly).
- Fix: the three sites join "opencode" like the rest of the pipeline.

SECONDARY (miss-path parity): model_default's configured-but-unresolvable branch
served a synthetic stub {providerID:"Own", id:"glm-5.3"}; v2 Model.default()
(model.ts:260-266) serves `available.find(supportsText)` — the first text model of
the SAME ordering /api/model serves. Extracted location_model_entries + supports_text
(model.rs); both fallback paths now use it. (Also removed v2-divergent
"first model of the provider" or_else.)

GROUND TRUTH (ref beta.12, live probes, synthetic config):
- matched case (synth/synth-1): ref default = synth/synth-1 "Synth One"; OURS = same ✓
- mismatched case (Synth/synth-1): ref default = opencode/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-free
  (its catalog vintage's first available text model); OURS = opencode/fledge-alpha-free
  (OUR catalog vintage's first) — same semantics, different models.dev snapshot
  (ref live-fetches; ours vendors). The providerID case miss is v2.0.24 behavior
  (byProvider.get exact match, model.ts:263) — kept 1:1, NOT "fixed" case-insensitively.
- user's real shape: ref lists own/{glm-5.3,glm-5.3-flash,gemini-3.8-flash,
  qwen3.8-flash-next}; OURS (fixed) lists the same 4 ✓; both default→fallback.
- NOT in scope (left): engine/mod.rs:761 global AGENTS.md discovery still uses the
  suffixed dir; models.dev snapshot vintage drift (ref live vs ours vendored).

